The cuboid is \(4\) cubes long, \(2\) cubes deep, and \(2\) cubes high.

Looking at the top faces, the white cubes occupy three consecutive positions along one edge, with a fourth white cube immediately behind one end:

\[
\begin{array}{cccc}
\text{dark} & \text{white} & \text{black} & \text{black}\\
\text{dark} & \text{white} & \text{white} & \text{white}
\end{array}
\]

Thus the white piece consists of four cubes arranged as an \(L\)-shape: three cubes in a straight line and one cube attached perpendicularly at an end. This matches choice \(E\).

\[
\boxed{\text{E}}
\]
